      ],
      "source": "https://www.lahabraca.gov/531/History",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1913, La Habra had become a 'tent city' as oil and citrus workers flooded in.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lahabraca.gov/531/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s name came from its first post office, which opened in a corner store in 1896.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
